cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this reproducibility package, please cite both the archived
  software/data package and the associated manuscript.
title: >-
  Reproducibility package for "Multi-timescale PTM architecture in human
  RNA polymerase II"
abstract: >-
  Human RNA polymerase II (Pol II) carries an extensive landscape of post-translational
  modifications (PTMs) and conformational states that collectively coordinate transcription
  and co-transcriptional RNA processing. Here, we compile residue-level annotations across
  the twelve human Pol II subunits and formulate an explicit discrete-state framework for
  the C-terminal domain, the non-CTD region of Rpb1, and subunits Rpb2–Rpb12. Under an
  independent-site construction, the curated residue-state landscape has a maximum logarithmic
  state-space size of 707.98 bits per Pol II molecule, including 211.22 bits contributed by the CTD.
  Experimental human CTD mass-spectrometry data support the five canonical phosphoacceptor-position
  classes represented in the framework and show qualitative agreement between the predominant
  Ser5-P and Ser2-P classes and the largest modeled position-class contributions. Empirical
  kinetic observations further support a multi-timescale architecture spanning seconds to hours.
  The quantitative framework distinguishes model-defined state-space size from physiological entropy
  and provides a reproducible approach to PTM-rich regulatory systems.
